WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.583
Episode three: check the cost, then run part of it.

2
00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:10.468
This video assumes APEX installed, as in episode one, and the copy my_first_case from episode two.

3
00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:16.330
Run every command below from the APEX folder.

4
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:29.294
File names in a configuration are relative to the configuration's own folder, so the copy reads its own files.

5
00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:34.325
This command prints everything such a file may hold, as a long JSON Schema.

6
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:50.613
We look only at its end.

7
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:52.390
Before running, the cost.

8
00:00:52.390 --> 00:01:04.748
The prior is the ensemble, 500 members drawn from a standard normal distribution.

9
00:01:04.748 --> 00:01:16.723
The method is ES-MDA in 4 steps (inflation = [4, 4, 4, 4]).

10
00:01:16.723 --> 00:01:22.368
apex validate checks the configuration without running anything, and prints the run's plan.

11
00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:40.093
Note that your run's id, a hash of the configuration and its folder, will differ.

12
00:01:40.093 --> 00:01:45.146
A forecast runs every member once: the prior's and one after each of the 4 steps.

13
00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:51.651
On a real case, the plan tells you the cost before you start.

14
00:01:51.651 --> 00:01:53.994
Now we run it, but only part of it.

15
00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:56.939
--max-steps 2 stops the run after two steps.

16
00:01:56.939 --> 00:02:14.646
The table shows the data mismatch falling from the prior (step 0).

17
00:02:14.646 --> 00:02:23.070
The run's folder is my_first_case/runs/linear_esmda, next to its configuration.

18
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:26.473
Every step is saved as a checkpoint in the run's folder.

19
00:02:26.473 --> 00:02:32.793
A long run can also be stopped from another terminal with this command: it stops at its next checkpoint.

20
00:02:32.793 --> 00:02:43.394
Ours has already stopped, so we only type it.

21
00:02:43.394 --> 00:02:46.476
So: validate first, and read the plan's cost.

22
00:02:46.476 --> 00:02:48.598
Max steps stops a run part-way.

23
00:02:48.598 --> 00:02:54.859
In the next video we resume it and read the results.

24
00:02:54.859 --> 00:03:00.359
Thank you for watching.
